    "body": "STOPPED at Step 5. Claim released. No production code changed.\n\nUpstream/main is 4e7929dfe4b5bae9d1f5154e8e48c40e675d8b1c. It has no RadialHeights, band_trim, or the_stated_radial_heights_move_the_generated_path test.\n\nThe reported test uses the held #2774 branch, FlamingFireCoding:issue/2774-rotary-heights, at 815075be7. That code clips the path to radial heights before it rebuilds the links. Main does not contain that feature.\n\nI added a temporary control test, rotary_parallel_fine_stepover_verifies_without_radial_band, to the existing rotary_verify fixture. It uses the laid bar, BN-0600, and a 0.5 mm stepover. It keeps main's existing height settings. It checks the operation status and blocking warnings.\n\nThe control passes on unchanged upstream/main: 1 passed, 0 failed. The targeted gate has 1 green step. This does not prove that #3490 is fixed. It does not exercise the held radial clipping code.\n\nThe overlap check found #3674 in rotary_parallel_over and the rotary_verify fixtures. I created the issue branch from that PR. Its unbanded control also passes. The first test build there failed because its older fixture lacked world_with. That compile error is not a reproduction of this defect.\n\nI could not establish the required failing pin on main. I stopped before a fix, mutation checks, or the full gates. No PR or commit was made. The temporary test and worktree are removed. The exact reproduction needs the held radial-band implementation.\n",
